  "name": "TWAS-XCAL: ancestry-aware calibration for transcriptome-wide association studies",
  "description": "Research software and benchmarks for ancestry-aware TWAS calibration under polygenic backgrounds. XCAL-t uses ancestry-matched LD, a finite-panel variance estimator and an approximate t reference. Counted simulation errors, model-based genotype-only predictions and a descriptive Biobank Japan application are distinguished. Current source is maintenance development version 0.3.1.dev0; the reported scientific analyses remain archived as v0.3.0, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24062489.",
